<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="160" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Budget inquiry: the shared EmailComposer in compose-only mode, To from the outside firm, a record link chosen by recipient, and a footer that names the record (D-179, D-181, UAT round 1)</title>
    <phase>11 UAT</phase>
    <gate>startable (D-179, D-181, owner 2026-10-22)</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <status-note>Steps 1-3 done on task/160-budget-inquiry-composer (PR open). Step 4 (merge, dev BFF + Console deploy, dev check of the three recipient cases) PENDING, main session.</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Shared UI component + wizard (.tsx) and BFF send path (.cs); touches an R3-owned file (GrantAccessNotifier).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting: composer contract, plan DTO, the inquiry send path, the reply-correlation footer and an external link builder owned by another project.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <deps>105 (UAT round 1); 158 (side-pane recipient lookup through the same host injection)</deps>
    <tags>bff,api,frontend,react,fluent-ui,email,testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
    <parallel-group>K</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Owner UAT round 1 (notes/uat-v4-log.md findings 5 and 7). The Send budget inquiry step uses plain Text fields: To does not look anything up, and it is not the shared email component. The email that was sent (address typed by hand) had no link to the record and came from the user's mailbox, which is correct per D-179. Its footer showed a raw `sprk_servicerequest {guid}` and a long `Ref:` token. D-179: use the shared EmailComposer in compose-only mode (nothing is sent until Record decision; the BFF sends at commit, from the deciding user's mailbox), with a recipient lookup and To pre-filled from the matter's outside-firm contact. D-181: the email links to its record by recipient. Internal users get the Spaarke app link. External contacts get the portal deep link `{PortalUrl}/?customer={key}&amp;record={type}:{id}`, which shows the portal's denied state when the record is outside their access. The footer names the record; the Ref token stays.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack engineer (decision wizard + Signals send path).</role>
  <goal>The budget-inquiry step renders the shared EmailComposer (compose-only, plain text, host-owned chrome, side-pane recipient lookup, To pre-filled). Its values commit in the shape the executor already accepts. The sent email carries the right record link for its recipients, and its footer reads the record's name and number.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Catalog: `send-budget-inquiry` (DecisionActionCatalog.cs:136) has to, subject and body (required) and outsideFirm (Lookup sprk_organization). Recipients are split on `; , space newline tab` (DecisionActionExecutors.cs:877, :1256), and an entry may be an address, a contact id or a law-firm id (MessageExecutorBase :820). Send path: BudgetInquiryActionExecutor (:1216) → BudgetInquiryExecutor (Actions/BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs:110) → InquiryEmailSender (:55) → `CommunicationService.SendAsync`, SendMode.User. `Build` (:77-90) sends plain text with ONE association, the sprk_servicerequest with no EntityName. CommunicationService.ApplyTrackingFooterAsync (:155-220) then prints `{EntityType} {EntityId}` (:189-191). The first association is the reply-correlation anchor and must stay the service request. send-reminder already falls back to the subject's `sprk_assignedlawfirm1` → primary contact email (report §2), which is the outside-firm contact resolver to reuse.
      EmailComposer (Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer, EmailComposer.types.ts): mode 'compose'; `hostOwnsChrome` (:636); `initialBodyFormat` 'PlainText' (:390); `sendMode` locks the From mode (:554); `onLookupRecipients(field)` for the side-pane lookup (:490); `onStateChange` (:575); `onSent`/`onSaveDraftRequest` are the send paths, which this task must not trigger.
      Links: the app record URL shape is `/main.aspx?etn={logical}&amp;id={id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord` (GrantAccessNotifier.cs:533). The portal link builder is `GrantAccessNotifier.BuildPortalLink(portalUrl, customerKey, ExternalGrantRootType, id)` (:412), which accepts only Project, Matter and WorkAssignment. The SPA parses `?record={type}:{id}` in `src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDeepLink.tsx` (R3 task 055); its parser is the authority for which type tokens exist. GrantAccessNotifier and the external SPA are R3's code.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DecisionWizard/steps/ActionStepView.tsx and ParameterFields.tsx (where the step renders parameters)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DecisionWizard/templatedDrafts.ts (D-53 templated subject/body)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.tsx and EmailComposer.types.ts</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (:234 DecisionPlanResponse, DecisionActionDto)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs (:55, :77-90, :110)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs:155-220 (footer; read only unless a change is unavoidable)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/GrantAccessNotifier.cs:393-430 (BuildPortalLink; R3-owned)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDeepLink.tsx (token set; R3-owned; read only)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <justification>
    <existing>EmailComposer is the shared composer; GrantAccessNotifier already builds both link shapes; the footer already prints EntityName when given.</existing>
    <extension>Adds one action-level presentation hint on the plan DTO (`composer: "email"` for the to/subject/body actions) and an optional `prefill` for To. The composer gains no new send path: it is used with host-owned chrome and onStateChange. The link builder gains a token-based overload next to the enum one, with no second builder.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Reviewers type addresses by hand in a non-standard form. The outside firm gets an email with no way to open the record, and a footer that shows a logical name and a GUID.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-10-23">Owner decisions 2026-10-23 amend the constraints below (each amended line says so): (1) an opt-in `composeOnly` prop on the shared EmailComposer, no fork, hostOwnsChrome unchanged, the shared-component diff in its own commit for the email project and R3 to review; (2) an ENABLED systemuser (sprk_isexternal included) gets the app link, anyone else the portal link, so a contact and a systemuser sharing an address is not a STOP; (3a) `to` is committed as ADDRESSES (the executor does not resolve contact ids); (3b) the app link is absolute, Dataverse:EnvironmentUrl + /main.aspx?etn=&amp;id=&amp;pagetype=entityrecord; (3c) the footer EntityName is "{core name} ({core number})" with NO "Budget inquiry:" prefix, because it is also sprk_regardingrecordname; (3d) the name and number are read at send time as the BFF; (3e) only the matter core the commit route supplies is supported.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-179">Compose-only: the composer in the wizard never sends, saves a draft, or creates a sprk_communication. It renders with hostOwnsChrome and (owner 2026-10-23) the opt-in `composeOnly` prop, which hides Send, the From row and static From text, and the Internal Only / External tags, and makes the composer's own send() and saveDraft() refuse with no network call; mode 'compose', plain text. The wizard reads To, Cc (if shown), Subject and Body through onStateChange into the step's values. The commit route and executor are the only send.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-179">To accepts recipients from the side-pane lookup (onLookupRecipients → host openLookup, contacts; same injection as task 158) and typed addresses. Values are committed in the existing `to` string shape (entries joined with "; "); owner 2026-10-23: the entries are the composer's email ADDRESSES, because BudgetInquiryActionExecutor.Map passes `to` unchanged to InquiryEmailSender.Build. No new parameter kind and no change to ReadValues' scalar rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-179">To pre-fill: the plan route returns, for send-budget-inquiry only, the outside-firm contact resolved AS THE CALLER with the same resolver send-reminder uses. If none resolves, To starts empty. A pre-fill the caller cannot read is never returned.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-53">Subject and body keep their templated drafts. No AI drafting (the composer's AI draft actions are not wired).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">send-reminder and send-email also declare composer "email" and so render the same composer. Their server send, recipients fallback and links are unchanged in this task (must-not-fire). If that widens the client change unsafely, STOP and ask.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-181">Link by recipient, decided at send time on the server. A recipient is internal when its address belongs to an enabled systemuser in the tenant (owner 2026-10-23: INCLUDING a systemuser flagged sprk_isexternal; an enabled systemuser wins over a contact with the same address); otherwise it is external. All internal → one line with the app link. All external → one line with the portal link. Mixed → both lines, each labelled for its audience. The link names the CORE record (matter, project or other core type), not the service request.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-181">Portal link: reuse GrantAccessNotifier's validation by adding an overload that takes the portal's type token. The enum overload calls it, so its behaviour is unchanged. Tokens come only from RecordDeepLink.tsx's parser. A core type the portal does not parse, no customer key, or an unusable PortalUrl gives no external link (logged at Warning). The email still sends. R3 reviews the GrantAccessNotifier change before merge (owner 2026-10-23: the main session routes the review; the implementer does not message peers).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-181">Footer: Build sets EntityName on the service-request association to "{core name} ({core number})" (name only if there is no number); owner 2026-10-23: NO "Budget inquiry:" prefix, because EntityName is also written to sprk_communication.sprk_regardingrecordname, which must name the record. The name and number are read at send time as the BFF. The association order is unchanged (reply correlation). CommunicationService is not edited unless that proves impossible, and then only after asking.</constraint>
    <constraint source="OWASP LLM05 / email">Every value that reaches the email is plain text. Links are built only from configured base URLs plus a type token and a GUID, never from user-typed text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta, full ArchTests, no unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests; notify word-add-in, R3 and uac-r2 before and after the dev BFF and Console deploys.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Failing tests first. Server: DTO composer hint and prefill (resolved, none, unreadable); link lines for all-internal, all-external, mixed, unparsed type, and missing key or URL; footer EntityName; association order unchanged; enum BuildPortalLink output unchanged. Client: the composer renders for composer "email"; no send, draft or From controls; state flows to values; side-pane lookup fills To; prefill shown; Next disabled until to/subject/body are present.</step>
    <step order="2">Server changes, then client changes.</step>
    <step order="3">Send the GrantAccessNotifier diff to R3 for review; fix their findings.</step>
    <step order="4">PR into docs, merged to master; R3 deploys the dev BFF; the Console auto-deploys. On dev: send an inquiry to one internal user, one external contact, and both together (zz- matter); open each link as that user. Check the footer text and that a reply still resolves the inquiry (criterion 10). Delete the zz- rows.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The budget-inquiry step renders EmailComposer with no Send, Save draft or From control; nothing is sent or saved before Record decision; at commit exactly one email is sent from the deciding user's mailbox.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a matter with an outside-firm contact the caller can read, then To is pre-filled with it; with none or unreadable, To is empty.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given all-internal recipients, the body carries the app link and no portal link. Given all-external, the portal link `{PortalUrl}/?customer={key}&amp;record={token}:{id}` and no app link. Given mixed, both, labelled.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a core type the portal does not parse, or no customer key, then no portal line is added and the email still sends (Warning logged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The footer reads "{name} ({number})" (owner 2026-10-23: no prefix), never a logical name or GUID; the Ref token is present; the service request is still the first association, and a reply resolves the inquiry on dev.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GrantAccessNotifier's existing enum overload returns the same links as before for Project, Matter and WorkAssignment (must-not-fire).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">send-reminder and send-email send exactly as before (server tests unchanged and passing).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On dev, the three recipient cases are checked and recorded in notes/deploy-log.md and notes/uat-v4-log.md; zz- rows deleted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the cases above. Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If EmailComposer cannot run without a send handler, or hostOwnsChrome does not remove Send, STOP and report. Do not fork the composer. (Resolved owner 2026-10-23: hostOwnsChrome does not remove Send; the opt-in composeOnly prop does.)</trigger>
    <trigger>If R3 objects to the BuildPortalLink overload, STOP and bring both positions to the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>If internal and external cannot be told apart reliably from the address (for example a contact and a systemuser share it), STOP and ask the owner which wins. (Resolved owner 2026-10-23: an enabled systemuser wins.)</trigger>
  </escalation>

